### Emajens API tests (REST Client extension)
### With the extension installed, a "Send Request" link appears above
### each request. Requests are separated by ### lines.

# Base URL shared by all requests below. If your backend runs on a
# different port, this is the only line you need to change.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/emergencies

### 1. Create a new emergency report
### Expect: 201 with { success: true, data: { ... } }
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Medical",
  "description": "Student injured near the engineering block",
  "location": {
    "latitude": 6.5244,
    "longitude": 3.3792
  }
}

### 2. Get all emergency reports (newest first)
### Expect: 200 with { success: true, count: N, data: [ ... ] }
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 3. Get a single report by ID
### Uses a real _id copied from request 1's response.
### Expect: 200 with the report, or 404 if the ID does not exist.
GET {{baseUrl}}/6ac4cf83036f412df0147265

### 4. Negative test: malformed ID
### Expect: 400 with "Invalid report ID format"
GET {{baseUrl}}/not-a-real-id

### 5. Negative test: missing required fields
### Expect: 400 validation error (type and description are required)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": {
    "latitude": 6.5244,
    "longitude": 3.3792
  }
}
